All,

Consider this explanation of the two different stainless steel stiffeners f=
or PE pipe available from Harco.   They are for use with DI fittings and jo=
int restraint as well as Harco LIV's.

Stiffeners in the PE price sheet:

These stiffeners are made by Harco.  They are for IPS (OD controlled) PE pi=
pe.  They are one piece, made of 304 Stainless Steel, and have optimized le=
ngths to be used in Harco bells (fittings or valves) with knuckle restraint=
s.  They are currently available for diameters 2", 3" and 4".  4" clam shel=
l restraint may also be used.  If "old style" restraints are used the user =
must be sure the grip ring is located just off the face of the bell to be s=
ure that the grip ring is over the stiffened part of the pipe.  In the pict=
ure below you can see the "dimples" on the left end.  These catch the ID of=
 the pipe to hold the stiffener in place.  The user pushes the stiffener in=
to the end of the PE pipe so that the dimple end is flush with the inlet fa=
ce of the pipe.  These are optimized for low cost and ease of installation.=
  To order the customer must know he has IPS OD controlled PE pipe, the nom=
inal diameter, and the DR.  We do not currently have the ability to make st=
iffeners for 1 1/2"" but possibly could.  Contact me if there is a need.  W=
e do not currently have this design for diameters larger than 4".  For larg=
er diameters refer to the stiffeners appearing in the DI price sheet.  Thes=
e stiffeners appear in the PE price sheet because at the beginning they wer=
e associated with the PE Transition with Stiffener fitting appearing in the=
 PE price sheet but have for the most part displaced the transition.

[cid:image002.png@01D2CFF4.34D638B0][Description: PPT 002.jpg]

Stiffeners in the DI price sheet:

These stiffeners we buy out.  They can be had for IPS OD controlled PE pipe=
 or DIPS PE pipe.  They are two piece comprised of a split tube and a wedge=
.  Note the installation below.  They are longer than the stiffeners in the=
 PE price sheet.  They are made of 304 Stainless Steel.  They are available=
 from 2" to 18".  20" is available but not shown in the DI price sheet beca=
use we only go up to 18" fittings in the price sheet.  The DI price sheets =
show 1 =BD" but this is no longer available.  See comments on this size in =
the comments on the stiffeners in the PE price sheet above.  To order the c=
ustomer must know the type of pipe (IPS or DIPS), the nominal diameter, and=
 the DR.  These were the original stiffeners in our catalog.  They are in t=
he DI price sheet because they are associated with our DI fittings.  At the=
 time they were added we did not have a PE fitting product line.  They are =
optimized for maximum cost and difficulty of installation.  Expect complain=
ts.


[cid:image006.png@01D2CFF2.1FAA85B0]

